{"id":29647,"slug":"paris-is-burning","title":"Paris Is Burning","year":1990,"country":"United States","duration":76,"spine":1018,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29647-paris-is-burning","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/db018ea632f4576c8eb5e168bbf244a0/LSoJP2f4HIWyY4pBAuk8lnOO82jBCv_large.jpg","description":"\nWhere does voguing come from, and what, exactly, is throwing shade? This landmark documentary provides a vibrant snapshot of the 1980s through the eyes of New York City’s African American and Latinx Harlem drag-ball scene. Made over seven years, Paris Is Burning offers an intimate portrait of rival fashion “houses,” from fierce contests for trophies to house mothers offering sustenance in a world rampant with homophobia, transphobia, racism, AIDS, and poverty. Featuring legendary voguers, drag queens, and trans women—including Willi Ninja, Pepper LaBeija, Dorian Corey, and Venus Xtravaganza—Paris Is Burning brings it, celebrating the joy of movement, the force of eloquence, and the draw of community.Paris Is Burning was restored  by the UCLA Film & Television Archive in conjunction with Sundance Institute and Outfest UCLA Legacy Project. Preservation was funded by Sundance Institute, Outfest, and the Andrew J. Kuehn Jr. Foundation.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Jennie Livingston","slug":"jennie-livingston"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Dorian Corey","role":"Mother, House of Corey","slug":"dorian-corey"},{"actor":"Pepper LaBeija","role":"Mother, House of LaBeija","slug":"pepper-labeija"},{"actor":"Junior LaBeija","role":"House of LaBeija","slug":"junior-labeija"},{"actor":"Angie Xtravaganza","role":"Mother, House of Xtravaganza","slug":"angie-xtravaganza"},{"actor":"Venus Xtravaganza","role":"House of Xtravaganza","slug":"venus-xtravaganza"},{"actor":"Danni Xtravaganza","role":"House of Xtravaganza","slug":"danni-xtravaganza"},{"actor":"Carmen Xtravaganza","role":"House of Xtravaganza","slug":"carmen-xtravaganza"},{"actor